{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/60957-darkening-skies-worth-buying","id":60957,"title":"Darkening Skies: worth buying?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-01-29T11:55:40-08:00","id":60957,"title":"Darkening Skies: worth buying?","content":"What the subject says. I\u2019m looking for spoilers to entice me to pick this up; so anyone who\u2019s bought it, please spoil away.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-29T12:49:42-08:00","id":60999,"title":"","content":"Purchased it. Have been skimming through it for the past hour or so. The writing is great, and the art is fantastic. But I'm mainly an Inquisitor player, so I'm satisfied. I'd say yes. Also, it's pretty cheap so I say go for it.<br /> <br /> I think I said yes, twice.<br /> <br /> Just buy it!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-29T13:38:43-08:00","id":61027,"title":"","content":"I've only really gone through the Fae section. If you're a Changeling fan, it details how the shattering happened.<br /> <br /> The downside is that the event is pretty underwhelming. It's all about a squabble between two fae who have never been mentioned before. To top it off, the whole thing is just an escort mission. I love the idea of weaponized banality causing the realm of faerie and earth to separate. I just wish the story around it had more weight.<br /> <br /> Edit to add: This is an event that is *huge* in DA: Fae and Changeling: The Dreaming - the fall of the Oath Truce and the Shattering. If anything should be treated as go big or go home, this is it. This should be something that should be a huge turning point in a DA: Fae game or something that could have ramifications all the way up to the modern day for Changeling games. Instead, the whole thing is boring and mundane. Such wasted potential.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Charlie Cantrell</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer <hr />Changeling: The Dreaming 20th Anniversary Edition, Conquering Heroes, Book of Freeholds, Guide to the Night, C20 Players Guide","edited":{"userid":648,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","user":"PookaKnight","date":". 01-29-2014, 04:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","name":"PookaKnight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"690"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-29T14:29:02-08:00","id":61063,"title":"","content":"Can someone spoil me on if there is any modification on the abilities list?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":412,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/412-valismedsen","user":"valismedsen","date":". 01-29-2014, 05:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/412-valismedsen","name":"valismedsen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar412_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"391"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-29T14:53:01-08:00","id":61086,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PookaKnight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/60957-darkening-skies-worth-buying?p=61027#post61027\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've only really gone through the Fae section. If you're a Changeling fan, it details how the shattering happened.<br /> <br /> The downside is that the event is pretty underwhelming. It's all about a squabble between two fae who have never been mentioned before. To top it off, the whole thing is just an escort mission. I love the idea of weaponized banality causing the realm of faerie and earth to separate. I just wish the story around it had more weight.<br /> <br /> Edit to add: This is an event that is *huge* in DA: Fae and Changeling: The Dreaming - the fall of the Oath Truce and the Shattering. If anything should be treated as go big or go home, this is it. This should be something that should be a huge turning point in a DA: Fae game or something that could have ramifications all the way up to the modern day for Changeling games. Instead, the whole thing is boring and mundane. Such wasted potential.</div> </div> </div> </div>Interesting. That implies that if the new Dark Ages line (which is set well after the 1230 eclipse) gets a Fae supplement, it\u2019s going to have to be very different from its predecessor: more of an \u201cin the wake of the recent calamity, we struggle to survive in a hostile world\u201d almost post-apocalyptic tone to it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-29T15:25:54-08:00","id":61108,"title":"","content":"Haven't gotten the pdf. yet, but you can see at least thirteen pages in the &quot;Preview&quot; thing DTRPG has. For Werewolf: Looks like the Stargazers are coming in thanks to the Mongol invasion. A tribe that the Red Talons didn't have any omens about or see them coming.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Rage CCG Collector and Artist. Visit the <a href=\"http://rageccg.proboards.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Rage CCG Forums</a>.<br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img818/5825/w20supportercliath125.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img839/9002/ylxu.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1137-laughing-hyena","name":"Laughing Hyena","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-29T20:30:08-08:00","id":61275,"title":"","content":"It sounds interesting. I'll be waiting for Drive-Thru RPG to release the physical copies before I get it. (They're not reprinting some of the newer and older stuff.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my DriveThruRPG books at: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?author=Carrie%20Kube\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse....=Carrie%20Kube</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1834-yaoi-huntress-earth","name":"Yaoi Huntress Earth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1834_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"535"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-29T21:22:13-08:00","id":61295,"title":"","content":"Word from someone else is that the Vampire bit is set in Seville and focuses on some ancient Vampire being awakened by some Lasombra (with Baali help, of course). Problem is, he can't be injured. There's apparently a lot of factions running about and the story is much more complicated than just &quot;fight the elder.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-30T03:16:04-08:00","id":61432,"title":"","content":"On my phone so I'll keep this short. I'm rather dissappointed to hear they dropped the ball in the single most important event in Fae history. Still I'd like to hear if the book has any new mechanics? For example something to bridge the gap between DAF and CtD. Or is the book only about stories/adventures?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","name":"Possessed","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1629_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-30T06:33:03-08:00","id":61502,"title":"","content":"Yeah, it was a really disappointing read. The adventure is everything people criticize Lord of the Rings about - nothing but walking and talking and walking some more. The difference is Lord of the Rings does more than that. When you're finally done walking, you get to watch a couple of NPCs you've never heard of maybe fight, or maybe not. The adventure actually says that it's entirely up to the ST if they fight or not.<br /> <br /> At least in the Fae chapter, it's almost entirely adventure and very little new mechanics. From a skim through, the other chapters are similar. The Fae section has two new treasures - one is a cage that's bigger on the inside. It's ok, if fairly pedestrian by fae standards. The other one is super cool. It's a fantastic idea that I wish the rest of the Fae chapter lived up to. It's the weapons that caused the Shattering - the fae equivalent of an atomic bomb. They're essentially weaponized banality, even if the Fae of the Dark Ages don't realize it. They're a magical necklace bathed in a priest's blood. When worn by a former changeling who has been baptized, if an unleashing happens in their presence the unleashing is nullified, the former changeling dies horribly, fae magic no longer works in the area, changelings no longer have access to their fae mien, inanimae can not access their greater features, and first born can not use the mists to hide themselves.<br /> <br /> <b>Edit to add:</b> As for Dataweaver and Possessed's questions about the long term fallout, if they do a new DA: Fae for V20 Dark Ages, the Oath-Truce would no longer be in effect, but it makes it sound like it takes quite a bit of time for the Shattering to fully play out. There could be areas that are pretty much DA: Fae status quo while other areas could be faerie no man's land. Here is everything on the transition between DA: Fae and Changeling: The Dreaming -<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> With the imposition of order and structure, the fae themselves become less varied, taking on Features similar to one another that are shaped by the dreams and nightmares of humanity. This gives rise to different kiths of changelings. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Charlie Cantrell</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer <hr />Changeling: The Dreaming 20th Anniversary Edition, Conquering Heroes, Book of Freeholds, Guide to the Night, C20 Players Guide","edited":{"userid":648,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","user":"PookaKnight","date":". 01-30-2014, 09:47 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","name":"PookaKnight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"690"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-30T10:58:12-08:00","id":61618,"title":"","content":"Word on mechanics from someone who has the book (again, not me): Vampire chapter has five new Devotions, while Inquisitor has a system for something called 'dramatic travel.'","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-30T11:06:07-08:00","id":61623,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/60957-darkening-skies-worth-buying?p=61618#post61618\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Word on mechanics from someone who has the book (again, not me): Vampire chapter has five new Devotions, while Inquisitor has a system for something called 'dramatic travel.'</div> </div> </div> </div>Dramatic Travel, for what it's worth, is a trial run for something we were going to test out for the V20 Dark Ages dramatic systems chapter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-30T12:10:21-08:00","id":61663,"title":"","content":"A banality bomb? Wow... I'm not really a CtD or DAF fan but that sounds cool. Still haven't completely decided if I'll get it but it does sound more and more interesting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-30T15:27:13-08:00","id":61778,"title":"","content":"I'm still reading through it, but I have to say: I love that cover. Nun blasting a vampire with lightning from a cross! Definitely Dark Fantastic.<br /> <br /> Since there isn't an errata thread, I'll just mention one oddity I found. Page 45 references a &quot;Paradox backlash.&quot; If I recall, In this time period, Mages who botch their effects suffer the &quot;scourge&quot;, which is sometimes seen as the wrath of God. Paradox backlashes generated by willworking against the dominant paradigm did not occur until some centuries later, as depicted in &quot;Mage: the Sorcerers Crusade.&quot; <br /> <br /> I know, it's kind of a pedantic complaint. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: the Ascension - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1191028-redesigned-prime-sphere\" target=\"_blank\">Redesigned Prime Sphere</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1188769-simpler-wonder-creation\" target=\"_blank\">Streamlined Wonder Creation</a><br /> Mummy: the Curse - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/474927-mummy-the-curse-2e-conversion\" target=\"_blank\">Lightweight 2E Conversion</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/22378-second-sight-tradition-disciples-of-duat\" target=\"_blank\">Disciples of Duat</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/61-octavo","name":"Octavo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar61_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-30T15:57:02-08:00","id":61802,"title":"","content":"Actually you have that mixed up. During the Dark Ages Paradox was commonly known as Backlash. In Sorcerer's Crusade it was known as Scourge, seen by some as the wrath of God. Of course more Christian leaning mages in the Dark Ages would have likely seen Backlash in the same light.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-30T16:20:41-08:00","id":61814,"title":"","content":"Ah, I think you're right.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: the Ascension - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1191028-redesigned-prime-sphere\" target=\"_blank\">Redesigned Prime Sphere</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1188769-simpler-wonder-creation\" target=\"_blank\">Streamlined Wonder Creation</a><br /> Mummy: the Curse - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/474927-mummy-the-curse-2e-conversion\" target=\"_blank\">Lightweight 2E Conversion</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/22378-second-sight-tradition-disciples-of-duat\" target=\"_blank\">Disciples of Duat</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/61-octavo","name":"Octavo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar61_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-01T13:01:14-08:00","id":63066,"title":"","content":"Broke down and bought the PDF. So far it's not bad. However I'm not too pleased with the font size of most of the pages. It's a bit on the small size.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akat